---
title: How to Debug Common Router Issues
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This guide covers debugging common TanStack Router problems, from route matching failures to navigation issues and performance problems."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick Start"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use TanStack Router DevTools for real-time debugging, add strategic console logging, and follow systematic troubleshooting patterns to identify and resolve router issues quickly."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"essential-debugging-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Essential Debugging Tools"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"1-tanstack-router-devtools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. TanStack Router DevTools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install and configure the DevTools for the best debugging experience:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/router-devtools","lang":"bash"},{"type":"code","value":"// src/App.tsx\nimport { TanStackRouterDevtools } from '@tanstack/router-devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <RouterProvider router={router} />\n      {/* Only shows in development */}\n      <TanStackRouterDevtools router={router} />\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DevTools Features:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route Tree Visualization"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - See your entire route structure"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current Route State"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Inspect active route data, params, and search"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Navigation History"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Track navigation events and timing"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route Matching"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - See which routes match current URL"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Performance Metrics"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Monitor route load times and re-renders"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"2-debug-mode-configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Debug Mode Configuration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enable debug mode for detailed console logging:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  defaultPreload: 'intent',\n  context: {\n    // your context\n  },\n  // Enable debug mode\n  debug: true,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"3-browser-devtools-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Browser DevTools Setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add router to global scope for debugging:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// In development only\nif (import.meta.env.DEV) {\n  window.router = router\n}\n\n// Console debugging commands:\n// router.state - current router state\n// router.navigate() - programmatic navigation\n// router.history - navigation history","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"route-matching-issues","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route Matching Issues"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"problem-route-not-found-404","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem: Route Not Found (404)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Symptoms:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route exists but shows 404 or \"Not Found\""}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Console shows route matching failures"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging Steps:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check Route Path Definition"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ Common mistake - missing leading slash\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: 'about', // Should be '/about'\n  // ...\n})\n\n// ✅ Correct\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/about',\n  // ...\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":2,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verify Route Tree Structure"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Debug route tree in console\nconsole.log('Route tree:', router.routeTree)\nconsole.log('All routes:', router.routesById)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":3,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check Parent Route Configuration"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Ensure parent route is properly defined\nconst childRoute = createRoute({\n  getParentRoute: () => parentRoute, // Must return correct parent\n  path: '/child',\n  // ...\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"problem-route-parameters-not-working","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem: Route Parameters Not Working"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Symptoms:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useParams()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns undefined or wrong values"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route params not being parsed correctly"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging Steps:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verify Parameter Syntax"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ Wrong parameter syntax\npath: '/users/{id}' // Should use $\n\n// ✅ Correct parameter syntax\npath: '/users/$userId'","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":2,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check Parameter Parsing"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"const route = createRoute({\n  path: '/users/$userId',\n  // Add parameter validation/parsing\n  params: {\n    parse: (params) => ({\n      userId: Number(params.userId), // Convert to number\n    }),\n    stringify: (params) => ({\n      userId: String(params.userId), // Convert back to string\n    }),\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    const { userId } = Route.useParams()\n    console.log('User ID:', userId, typeof userId) // Debug output\n    return <div>User {userId}</div>\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":3,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debug Current URL and Params"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"function DebugParams() {\n  const location = useLocation()\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n\n  console.log('Current pathname:', location.pathname)\n  console.log('Parsed params:', params)\n\n  return null // Just for debugging\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"navigation-issues","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Navigation Issues"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"problem-navigation-not-working","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem: Navigation Not Working"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Symptoms:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Links don't navigate"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Programmatic navigation fails silently"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser URL doesn't update"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging Steps:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check Link Configuration"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ Common mistakes\n<Link to=\"about\">About</Link> // Missing leading slash\n<Link href=\"/about\">About</Link> // Wrong prop (href instead of to)\n\n// ✅ Correct\n<Link to=\"/about\">About</Link>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":2,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debug Navigation Calls"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"function NavigationDebug() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n\n  const handleNavigate = () => {\n    console.log('Attempting navigation...')\n    navigate({\n      to: '/dashboard',\n      search: { tab: 'settings' },\n    })\n      .then(() => console.log('Navigation successful'))\n      .catch((err) => console.error('Navigation failed:', err))\n  }\n\n  return <button onClick={handleNavigate}>Navigate</button>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":3,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check Router Context"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Ensure component is inside RouterProvider\nfunction ComponentWithNavigation() {\n  const router = useRouter() // Will throw error if outside provider\n  console.log('Router state:', router.state)\n\n  return <div>...</div>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"problem-navigation-redirects-unexpectedly","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem: Navigation Redirects Unexpectedly"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Symptoms:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Navigating to one route but ending up somewhere else"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Infinite redirect loops"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging Steps:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check Route Guards"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"const route = createRoute({\n  path: '/dashboard',\n  beforeLoad: ({ context, location }) => {\n    console.log('Before load - location:', location.pathname)\n    console.log('Auth state:', context.auth)\n\n    if (!context.auth.isAuthenticated) {\n      console.log('Redirecting to login...')\n      throw redirect({ to: '/login' })\n    }\n  },\n  // ...\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":2,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debug Redirect Chains"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Add to router configuration\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    /* ... */\n  },\n  // Log all navigation events\n  onNavigate: ({ location, type }) => {\n    console.log(`Navigation (${type}):`, location.pathname)\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"data-loading-problems","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Data Loading Problems"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"problem-route-data-not-loading","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem: Route Data Not Loading"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Symptoms:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLoaderData()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns undefined"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Loading states not working correctly"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Data not refreshing"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging Steps:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check Loader Implementation"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"const route = createRoute({\n  path: '/posts',\n  loader: async ({ params, context }) => {\n    console.log('Loader called with params:', params)\n\n    try {\n      const data = await fetchPosts()\n      console.log('Loader data:', data)\n      return data\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error('Loader error:', error)\n      throw error\n    }\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    const data = Route.useLoaderData()\n    console.log('Component data:', data)\n\n    return <div>{/* render data */}</div>\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":2,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debug Loading States"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"function DataLoadingDebug() {\n  const state = useRouterState()\n\n  console.log('Route status:', {\n    status: state.status,\n    isLoading: state.isLoading,\n    matches: state.matches.map((match) => ({\n      routeId: match.routeId,\n      status: match.status,\n      isFetching: match.isFetching,\n    })),\n  })\n\n  return null\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":3,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check Loader Dependencies"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"const route = createRoute({\n  path: '/posts/$postId',\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    // Loader will re-run when params change\n    console.log('Loading post:', params.postId)\n    return fetchPost(params.postId)\n  },\n  // Add dependencies for explicit re-loading\n  loaderDeps: ({ search }) => ({\n    refresh: search.refresh,\n  }),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"search-parameters-issues","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Search Parameters Issues"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"problem-search-params-not-updating","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem: Search Params Not Updating"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Symptoms:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"URL search params don't update"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSearch()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns stale data"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Search validation errors"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging Steps:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check Search Validation Schema"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"const route = createRoute({\n  path: '/search',\n  validateSearch: (search) => {\n    console.log('Raw search params:', search)\n\n    const validated = {\n      q: (search.q as string) || '',\n      page: Number(search.page) || 1,\n    }\n\n    console.log('Validated search params:', validated)\n    return validated\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    const search = Route.useSearch()\n    console.log('Component search:', search)\n\n    return <div>Query: {search.q}</div>\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":2,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debug Search Navigation"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"function SearchDebug() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n  const currentSearch = Route.useSearch()\n\n  const updateSearch = (newSearch: any) => {\n    console.log('Current search:', currentSearch)\n    console.log('New search:', newSearch)\n\n    navigate({\n      to: '.',\n      search: (prev) => {\n        const updated = { ...prev, ...newSearch }\n        console.log('Final search:', updated)\n        return updated\n      },\n    })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <button onClick={() => updateSearch({ q: 'test' })}>Update Search</button>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"performance-issues","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Performance Issues"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"problem-excessive-re-renders","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem: Excessive Re-renders"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Symptoms:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Components re-rendering too often"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Performance lag during navigation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memory usage increasing"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging Steps:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use React DevTools Profiler"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Wrap your app for profiling\nimport { Profiler } from 'react'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <Profiler\n      id=\"Router\"\n      onRender={(id, phase, actualDuration) => {\n        console.log(`${id} ${phase} took ${actualDuration}ms`)\n      }}\n    >\n      <RouterProvider router={router} />\n    </Profiler>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":2,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optimize Route Subscriptions"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ Subscribes to all search params\nfunction MyComponent() {\n  const search = Route.useSearch()\n  return <div>{search.someSpecificField}</div>\n}\n\n// ✅ Subscribe only to specific field\nfunction MyComponent() {\n  const someSpecificField = Route.useSearch({\n    select: (search) => search.someSpecificField,\n  })\n  return <div>{someSpecificField}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":3,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Monitor Route State Changes"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Add to router configuration\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    /* ... */\n  },\n  onUpdate: (router) => {\n    console.log('Router state updated:', {\n      pathname: router.state.location.pathname,\n      isLoading: router.state.isLoading,\n      matches: router.state.matches.length,\n    })\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"problem-memory-leaks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem: Memory Leaks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Symptoms:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memory usage constantly increasing"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser becomes slow over time"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route components not cleaning up"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging Steps:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check Component Cleanup"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"function MyComponent() {\n  const [data, setData] = useState(null)\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const subscription = someService.subscribe(setData)\n\n    // ✅ Always clean up subscriptions\n    return () => {\n      subscription.unsubscribe()\n    }\n  }, [])\n\n  return <div>{data}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":2,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Monitor Route Unmounting"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"function DebuggableComponent() {\n  useEffect(() => {\n    console.log('Component mounted')\n\n    return () => {\n      console.log('Component unmounted')\n    }\n  }, [])\n\n  return <div>Content</div>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typescript-issues","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript Issues"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"problem-type-errors-with-router","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem: Type Errors with Router"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Symptoms:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript errors in route definitions"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type inference not working"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameter types incorrect"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging Steps:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check Route Tree Type Registration"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Ensure this declaration exists\ndeclare module '@tanstack/react-router' {\n  interface Register {\n    router: typeof router\n  }\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":2,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debug Route Type Generation"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"# Check if route types are being generated\nls src/routeTree.gen.ts\n\n# Regenerate route types if needed\nnpx @tanstack/router-cli generate","lang":"bash"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":3,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use Type Assertions for Debugging"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"function TypeDebugComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  const search = Route.useSearch()\n\n  // Add type assertions to check what TypeScript infers\n  console.log('Params type:', params as any)\n  console.log('Search type:', search as any)\n\n  return null\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"systematic-debugging-process","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Systematic Debugging Process"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"1-information-gathering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Information Gathering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When debugging any router issue, start by collecting this information:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function RouterDebugInfo() {\n  const router = useRouter()\n  const location = useLocation()\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    console.group('🐛 Router Debug Info')\n    console.log('Current pathname:', location.pathname)\n    console.log('Search params:', location.search)\n    console.log('Router state:', router.state)\n    console.log('Active matches:', router.state.matches)\n    console.log('Route tree:', router.routeTree)\n    console.groupEnd()\n  }, [location.pathname])\n\n  return null\n}\n\n// Add to your app during debugging\n;<RouterDebugInfo />","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"2-isolation-testing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Isolation Testing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create minimal reproduction:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Minimal route for testing\nconst testRoute = createRoute({\n  getParentRoute: () => rootRoute,\n  path: '/debug',\n  component: () => {\n    console.log('Test route rendered')\n    return <div>Debug Route</div>\n  },\n})\n\n// Add to route tree temporarily\nconst routeTree = rootRoute.addChildren([\n  // ... other routes\n  testRoute, // Add test route\n])","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"3-step-by-step-debugging","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Step-by-Step Debugging"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verify basic setup"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Router provider, route tree structure"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check route definitions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Paths, parent routes, configuration"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Test navigation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Links, programmatic navigation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validate data flow"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Loaders, search params, context"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Monitor performance"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Re-renders, memory usage"}]}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"browser-debugging-tips","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser Debugging Tips"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"console-commands","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Console Commands"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// In browser console (when router is on window)\n\n// Current router state\nrouter.state\n\n// Navigate programmatically\nrouter.navigate({ to: '/some-path' })\n\n// Get route by path\nrouter.getRoute('/users/$userId')\n\n// Check if route exists\nrouter.buildLocation({ to: '/some-path' })\n\n// View all registered routes\nObject.keys(router.routesById)","lang":"js"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"network-tab","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Network Tab"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Monitor these requests when debugging:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route code chunks"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Check if lazy routes are loading"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Loader data requests"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Verify API calls from loaders"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Failed requests"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Look for 404s or failed API calls"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"react-devtools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React DevTools"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Components Tab"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Find router components and inspect props"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Profiler Tab"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Identify performance bottlenecks"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Search for components"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Find specific route components quickly"}]}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-error-messages","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Error Messages"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"route-not-found","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"Route not found\""}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check route path spelling and case sensitivity"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verify route is added to route tree"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ensure parent routes are properly configured"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"cannot-read-property-useparams-of-undefined","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"Cannot read property 'useParams' of undefined\""}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component is likely outside RouterProvider"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route might not be properly registered"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check if using correct Route object"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"invalid-search-params","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"Invalid search params\""}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check validateSearch schema"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verify search param types match schema"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Look for required vs optional parameters"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"navigation-was-interrupted","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"Navigation was interrupted\""}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usually caused by redirect in beforeLoad"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check for redirect loops"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verify authentication logic"}]}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"performance-monitoring","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Performance Monitoring"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enable-performance-tracking","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enable Performance Tracking"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    /* ... */\n  },\n  onUpdate: (router) => {\n    performance.mark('router-update')\n  },\n  onLoad: (router) => {\n    performance.mark('router-load')\n    performance.measure('router-load-time', 'router-update', 'router-load')\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"monitor-route-loading-times","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Monitor Route Loading Times"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const route = createRoute({\n  path: '/slow-route',\n  loader: async () => {\n    const start = performance.now()\n    const data = await fetchData()\n    const end = performance.now()\n\n    console.log(`Loader took ${end - start}ms`)\n    return data\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Next Steps"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After debugging router issues, you might want to:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./setup-testing.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How to Set Up Testing"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Add tests to prevent regressions"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./deploy-to-production.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How to Deploy to Production"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Ensure issues don't occur in production"}]}]}]},{"type":"html","value":"<!-- TODO: Uncomment as guides are created\n- [How to Optimize Performance](./optimize-performance.md)\n- [How to Set Up Error Monitoring](./setup-error-monitoring.md)\n-->"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"related-resources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Related Resources"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/router/tree/main/packages/router-devtools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Router DevTools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Official debugging tools"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://react.dev/learn/react-developer-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React DevTools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - React-specific debugging"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../overview.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Router Core Documentation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Understanding router internals"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"quick-start","text":"Quick Start","level":2},{"id":"essential-debugging-tools","text":"Essential Debugging Tools","level":2},{"id":"1-tanstack-router-devtools","text":"1. TanStack Router DevTools","level":3},{"id":"2-debug-mode-configuration","text":"2. Debug Mode Configuration","level":3},{"id":"3-browser-devtools-setup","text":"3. Browser DevTools Setup","level":3},{"id":"route-matching-issues","text":"Route Matching Issues","level":2},{"id":"problem-route-not-found-404","text":"Problem: Route Not Found (404)","level":3},{"id":"problem-route-parameters-not-working","text":"Problem: Route Parameters Not Working","level":3},{"id":"navigation-issues","text":"Navigation Issues","level":2},{"id":"problem-navigation-not-working","text":"Problem: Navigation Not Working","level":3},{"id":"problem-navigation-redirects-unexpectedly","text":"Problem: Navigation Redirects Unexpectedly","level":3},{"id":"data-loading-problems","text":"Data Loading Problems","level":2},{"id":"problem-route-data-not-loading","text":"Problem: Route Data Not Loading","level":3},{"id":"search-parameters-issues","text":"Search Parameters Issues","level":2},{"id":"problem-search-params-not-updating","text":"Problem: Search Params Not Updating","level":3},{"id":"performance-issues","text":"Performance Issues","level":2},{"id":"problem-excessive-re-renders","text":"Problem: Excessive Re-renders","level":3},{"id":"problem-memory-leaks","text":"Problem: Memory Leaks","level":3},{"id":"typescript-issues","text":"TypeScript Issues","level":2},{"id":"problem-type-errors-with-router","text":"Problem: Type Errors with Router","level":3},{"id":"systematic-debugging-process","text":"Systematic Debugging Process","level":2},{"id":"1-information-gathering","text":"1. Information Gathering","level":3},{"id":"2-isolation-testing","text":"2. Isolation Testing","level":3},{"id":"3-step-by-step-debugging","text":"3. Step-by-Step Debugging","level":3},{"id":"browser-debugging-tips","text":"Browser Debugging Tips","level":2},{"id":"console-commands","text":"Console Commands","level":3},{"id":"network-tab","text":"Network Tab","level":3},{"id":"react-devtools","text":"React DevTools","level":3},{"id":"common-error-messages","text":"Common Error Messages","level":2},{"id":"route-not-found","text":"\"Route not found\"","level":3},{"id":"cannot-read-property-useparams-of-undefined","text":"\"Cannot read property 'useParams' of undefined\"","level":3},{"id":"invalid-search-params","text":"\"Invalid search params\"","level":3},{"id":"navigation-was-interrupted","text":"\"Navigation was interrupted\"","level":3},{"id":"performance-monitoring","text":"Performance Monitoring","level":2},{"id":"enable-performance-tracking","text":"Enable Performance Tracking","level":3},{"id":"monitor-route-loading-times","text":"Monitor Route Loading Times","level":3},{"id":"common-next-steps","text":"Common Next Steps","level":2},{"id":"related-resources","text":"Related Resources","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThis guide covers debugging common TanStack Router problems, from route matching failures to navigation issues and performance problems.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nUse TanStack Router DevTools for real-time debugging, add strategic console logging, and follow systematic troubleshooting patterns to identify and resolve router issues quickly.\n\n---\n\n## Essential Debugging Tools\n\n### 1. TanStack Router DevTools\n\nInstall and configure the DevTools for the best debugging experience:\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/router-devtools\n```\n\n```tsx\n// src/App.tsx\nimport { TanStackRouterDevtools } from '@tanstack/router-devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <RouterProvider router={router} />\n      {/* Only shows in development */}\n      <TanStackRouterDevtools router={router} />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n**DevTools Features:**\n\n- **Route Tree Visualization** - See your entire route structure\n- **Current Route State** - Inspect active route data, params, and search\n- **Navigation History** - Track navigation events and timing\n- **Route Matching** - See which routes match current URL\n- **Performance Metrics** - Monitor route load times and re-renders\n\n### 2. Debug Mode Configuration\n\nEnable debug mode for detailed console logging:\n\n```tsx\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  defaultPreload: 'intent',\n  context: {\n    // your context\n  },\n  // Enable debug mode\n  debug: true,\n})\n```\n\n### 3. Browser DevTools Setup\n\n**Add router to global scope for debugging:**\n\n```tsx\n// In development only\nif (import.meta.env.DEV) {\n  window.router = router\n}\n\n// Console debugging commands:\n// router.state - current router state\n// router.navigate() - programmatic navigation\n// router.history - navigation history\n```\n\n---\n\n## Route Matching Issues\n\n### Problem: Route Not Found (404)\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- Route exists but shows 404 or \"Not Found\"\n- Console shows route matching failures\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Check Route Path Definition**\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Common mistake - missing leading slash\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: 'about', // Should be '/about'\n  // ...\n})\n\n// ✅ Correct\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/about',\n  // ...\n})\n```\n\n2. **Verify Route Tree Structure**\n\n```tsx\n// Debug route tree in console\nconsole.log('Route tree:', router.routeTree)\nconsole.log('All routes:', router.routesById)\n```\n\n3. **Check Parent Route Configuration**\n\n```tsx\n// Ensure parent route is properly defined\nconst childRoute = createRoute({\n  getParentRoute: () => parentRoute, // Must return correct parent\n  path: '/child',\n  // ...\n})\n```\n\n### Problem: Route Parameters Not Working\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- `useParams()` returns undefined or wrong values\n- Route params not being parsed correctly\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Verify Parameter Syntax**\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Wrong parameter syntax\npath: '/users/{id}' // Should use $\n\n// ✅ Correct parameter syntax\npath: '/users/$userId'\n```\n\n2. **Check Parameter Parsing**\n\n```tsx\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/users/$userId',\n  // Add parameter validation/parsing\n  params: {\n    parse: (params) => ({\n      userId: Number(params.userId), // Convert to number\n    }),\n    stringify: (params) => ({\n      userId: String(params.userId), // Convert back to string\n    }),\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    const { userId } = Route.useParams()\n    console.log('User ID:', userId, typeof userId) // Debug output\n    return <div>User {userId}</div>\n  },\n})\n```\n\n3. **Debug Current URL and Params**\n\n```tsx\nfunction DebugParams() {\n  const location = useLocation()\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n\n  console.log('Current pathname:', location.pathname)\n  console.log('Parsed params:', params)\n\n  return null // Just for debugging\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Navigation Issues\n\n### Problem: Navigation Not Working\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- Links don't navigate\n- Programmatic navigation fails silently\n- Browser URL doesn't update\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Check Link Configuration**\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Common mistakes\n<Link to=\"about\">About</Link> // Missing leading slash\n<Link href=\"/about\">About</Link> // Wrong prop (href instead of to)\n\n// ✅ Correct\n<Link to=\"/about\">About</Link>\n```\n\n2. **Debug Navigation Calls**\n\n```tsx\nfunction NavigationDebug() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n\n  const handleNavigate = () => {\n    console.log('Attempting navigation...')\n    navigate({\n      to: '/dashboard',\n      search: { tab: 'settings' },\n    })\n      .then(() => console.log('Navigation successful'))\n      .catch((err) => console.error('Navigation failed:', err))\n  }\n\n  return <button onClick={handleNavigate}>Navigate</button>\n}\n```\n\n3. **Check Router Context**\n\n```tsx\n// Ensure component is inside RouterProvider\nfunction ComponentWithNavigation() {\n  const router = useRouter() // Will throw error if outside provider\n  console.log('Router state:', router.state)\n\n  return <div>...</div>\n}\n```\n\n### Problem: Navigation Redirects Unexpectedly\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- Navigating to one route but ending up somewhere else\n- Infinite redirect loops\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Check Route Guards**\n\n```tsx\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/dashboard',\n  beforeLoad: ({ context, location }) => {\n    console.log('Before load - location:', location.pathname)\n    console.log('Auth state:', context.auth)\n\n    if (!context.auth.isAuthenticated) {\n      console.log('Redirecting to login...')\n      throw redirect({ to: '/login' })\n    }\n  },\n  // ...\n})\n```\n\n2. **Debug Redirect Chains**\n\n```tsx\n// Add to router configuration\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    /* ... */\n  },\n  // Log all navigation events\n  onNavigate: ({ location, type }) => {\n    console.log(`Navigation (${type}):`, location.pathname)\n  },\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## Data Loading Problems\n\n### Problem: Route Data Not Loading\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- `useLoaderData()` returns undefined\n- Loading states not working correctly\n- Data not refreshing\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Check Loader Implementation**\n\n```tsx\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/posts',\n  loader: async ({ params, context }) => {\n    console.log('Loader called with params:', params)\n\n    try {\n      const data = await fetchPosts()\n      console.log('Loader data:', data)\n      return data\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error('Loader error:', error)\n      throw error\n    }\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    const data = Route.useLoaderData()\n    console.log('Component data:', data)\n\n    return <div>{/* render data */}</div>\n  },\n})\n```\n\n2. **Debug Loading States**\n\n```tsx\nfunction DataLoadingDebug() {\n  const state = useRouterState()\n\n  console.log('Route status:', {\n    status: state.status,\n    isLoading: state.isLoading,\n    matches: state.matches.map((match) => ({\n      routeId: match.routeId,\n      status: match.status,\n      isFetching: match.isFetching,\n    })),\n  })\n\n  return null\n}\n```\n\n3. **Check Loader Dependencies**\n\n```tsx\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/posts/$postId',\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    // Loader will re-run when params change\n    console.log('Loading post:', params.postId)\n    return fetchPost(params.postId)\n  },\n  // Add dependencies for explicit re-loading\n  loaderDeps: ({ search }) => ({\n    refresh: search.refresh,\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## Search Parameters Issues\n\n### Problem: Search Params Not Updating\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- URL search params don't update\n- `useSearch()` returns stale data\n- Search validation errors\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Check Search Validation Schema**\n\n```tsx\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/search',\n  validateSearch: (search) => {\n    console.log('Raw search params:', search)\n\n    const validated = {\n      q: (search.q as string) || '',\n      page: Number(search.page) || 1,\n    }\n\n    console.log('Validated search params:', validated)\n    return validated\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    const search = Route.useSearch()\n    console.log('Component search:', search)\n\n    return <div>Query: {search.q}</div>\n  },\n})\n```\n\n2. **Debug Search Navigation**\n\n```tsx\nfunction SearchDebug() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n  const currentSearch = Route.useSearch()\n\n  const updateSearch = (newSearch: any) => {\n    console.log('Current search:', currentSearch)\n    console.log('New search:', newSearch)\n\n    navigate({\n      to: '.',\n      search: (prev) => {\n        const updated = { ...prev, ...newSearch }\n        console.log('Final search:', updated)\n        return updated\n      },\n    })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <button onClick={() => updateSearch({ q: 'test' })}>Update Search</button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Performance Issues\n\n### Problem: Excessive Re-renders\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- Components re-rendering too often\n- Performance lag during navigation\n- Memory usage increasing\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Use React DevTools Profiler**\n\n```tsx\n// Wrap your app for profiling\nimport { Profiler } from 'react'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <Profiler\n      id=\"Router\"\n      onRender={(id, phase, actualDuration) => {\n        console.log(`${id} ${phase} took ${actualDuration}ms`)\n      }}\n    >\n      <RouterProvider router={router} />\n    </Profiler>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n2. **Optimize Route Subscriptions**\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Subscribes to all search params\nfunction MyComponent() {\n  const search = Route.useSearch()\n  return <div>{search.someSpecificField}</div>\n}\n\n// ✅ Subscribe only to specific field\nfunction MyComponent() {\n  const someSpecificField = Route.useSearch({\n    select: (search) => search.someSpecificField,\n  })\n  return <div>{someSpecificField}</div>\n}\n```\n\n3. **Monitor Route State Changes**\n\n```tsx\n// Add to router configuration\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    /* ... */\n  },\n  onUpdate: (router) => {\n    console.log('Router state updated:', {\n      pathname: router.state.location.pathname,\n      isLoading: router.state.isLoading,\n      matches: router.state.matches.length,\n    })\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Problem: Memory Leaks\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- Memory usage constantly increasing\n- Browser becomes slow over time\n- Route components not cleaning up\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Check Component Cleanup**\n\n```tsx\nfunction MyComponent() {\n  const [data, setData] = useState(null)\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const subscription = someService.subscribe(setData)\n\n    // ✅ Always clean up subscriptions\n    return () => {\n      subscription.unsubscribe()\n    }\n  }, [])\n\n  return <div>{data}</div>\n}\n```\n\n2. **Monitor Route Unmounting**\n\n```tsx\nfunction DebuggableComponent() {\n  useEffect(() => {\n    console.log('Component mounted')\n\n    return () => {\n      console.log('Component unmounted')\n    }\n  }, [])\n\n  return <div>Content</div>\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## TypeScript Issues\n\n### Problem: Type Errors with Router\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- TypeScript errors in route definitions\n- Type inference not working\n- Parameter types incorrect\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Check Route Tree Type Registration**\n\n```tsx\n// Ensure this declaration exists\ndeclare module '@tanstack/react-router' {\n  interface Register {\n    router: typeof router\n  }\n}\n```\n\n2. **Debug Route Type Generation**\n\n```bash\n# Check if route types are being generated\nls src/routeTree.gen.ts\n\n# Regenerate route types if needed\nnpx @tanstack/router-cli generate\n```\n\n3. **Use Type Assertions for Debugging**\n\n```tsx\nfunction TypeDebugComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  const search = Route.useSearch()\n\n  // Add type assertions to check what TypeScript infers\n  console.log('Params type:', params as any)\n  console.log('Search type:', search as any)\n\n  return null\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Systematic Debugging Process\n\n### 1. Information Gathering\n\nWhen debugging any router issue, start by collecting this information:\n\n```tsx\nfunction RouterDebugInfo() {\n  const router = useRouter()\n  const location = useLocation()\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    console.group('🐛 Router Debug Info')\n    console.log('Current pathname:', location.pathname)\n    console.log('Search params:', location.search)\n    console.log('Router state:', router.state)\n    console.log('Active matches:', router.state.matches)\n    console.log('Route tree:', router.routeTree)\n    console.groupEnd()\n  }, [location.pathname])\n\n  return null\n}\n\n// Add to your app during debugging\n;<RouterDebugInfo />\n```\n\n### 2. Isolation Testing\n\nCreate minimal reproduction:\n\n```tsx\n// Minimal route for testing\nconst testRoute = createRoute({\n  getParentRoute: () => rootRoute,\n  path: '/debug',\n  component: () => {\n    console.log('Test route rendered')\n    return <div>Debug Route</div>\n  },\n})\n\n// Add to route tree temporarily\nconst routeTree = rootRoute.addChildren([\n  // ... other routes\n  testRoute, // Add test route\n])\n```\n\n### 3. Step-by-Step Debugging\n\n1. **Verify basic setup** - Router provider, route tree structure\n2. **Check route definitions** - Paths, parent routes, configuration\n3. **Test navigation** - Links, programmatic navigation\n4. **Validate data flow** - Loaders, search params, context\n5. **Monitor performance** - Re-renders, memory usage\n\n---\n\n## Browser Debugging Tips\n\n### Console Commands\n\n```js\n// In browser console (when router is on window)\n\n// Current router state\nrouter.state\n\n// Navigate programmatically\nrouter.navigate({ to: '/some-path' })\n\n// Get route by path\nrouter.getRoute('/users/$userId')\n\n// Check if route exists\nrouter.buildLocation({ to: '/some-path' })\n\n// View all registered routes\nObject.keys(router.routesById)\n```\n\n### Network Tab\n\nMonitor these requests when debugging:\n\n- **Route code chunks** - Check if lazy routes are loading\n- **Loader data requests** - Verify API calls from loaders\n- **Failed requests** - Look for 404s or failed API calls\n\n### React DevTools\n\n1. **Components Tab** - Find router components and inspect props\n2. **Profiler Tab** - Identify performance bottlenecks\n3. **Search for components** - Find specific route components quickly\n\n---\n\n## Common Error Messages\n\n### \"Route not found\"\n\n- Check route path spelling and case sensitivity\n- Verify route is added to route tree\n- Ensure parent routes are properly configured\n\n### \"Cannot read property 'useParams' of undefined\"\n\n- Component is likely outside RouterProvider\n- Route might not be properly registered\n- Check if using correct Route object\n\n### \"Invalid search params\"\n\n- Check validateSearch schema\n- Verify search param types match schema\n- Look for required vs optional parameters\n\n### \"Navigation was interrupted\"\n\n- Usually caused by redirect in beforeLoad\n- Check for redirect loops\n- Verify authentication logic\n\n---\n\n## Performance Monitoring\n\n### Enable Performance Tracking\n\n```tsx\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    /* ... */\n  },\n  onUpdate: (router) => {\n    performance.mark('router-update')\n  },\n  onLoad: (router) => {\n    performance.mark('router-load')\n    performance.measure('router-load-time', 'router-update', 'router-load')\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Monitor Route Loading Times\n\n```tsx\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/slow-route',\n  loader: async () => {\n    const start = performance.now()\n    const data = await fetchData()\n    const end = performance.now()\n\n    console.log(`Loader took ${end - start}ms`)\n    return data\n  },\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Next Steps\n\nAfter debugging router issues, you might want to:\n\n- [How to Set Up Testing](./setup-testing.md) - Add tests to prevent regressions\n- [How to Deploy to Production](./deploy-to-production.md) - Ensure issues don't occur in production\n\n<!-- TODO: Uncomment as guides are created\n- [How to Optimize Performance](./optimize-performance.md)\n- [How to Set Up Error Monitoring](./setup-error-monitoring.md)\n-->\n\n## Related Resources\n\n- [TanStack Router DevTools](https://github.com/TanStack/router/tree/main/packages/router-devtools) - Official debugging tools\n- [React DevTools](https://react.dev/learn/react-developer-tools) - React-specific debugging\n- [Router Core Documentation](../overview.md) - Understanding router internals\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: How to Debug Common Router Issues\n---\n\nThis guide covers debugging common TanStack Router problems, from route matching failures to navigation issues and performance problems.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nUse TanStack Router DevTools for real-time debugging, add strategic console logging, and follow systematic troubleshooting patterns to identify and resolve router issues quickly.\n\n---\n\n## Essential Debugging Tools\n\n### 1. TanStack Router DevTools\n\nInstall and configure the DevTools for the best debugging experience:\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/router-devtools\n```\n\n```tsx\n// src/App.tsx\nimport { TanStackRouterDevtools } from '@tanstack/router-devtools'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <RouterProvider router={router} />\n      {/* Only shows in development */}\n      <TanStackRouterDevtools router={router} />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n**DevTools Features:**\n\n- **Route Tree Visualization** - See your entire route structure\n- **Current Route State** - Inspect active route data, params, and search\n- **Navigation History** - Track navigation events and timing\n- **Route Matching** - See which routes match current URL\n- **Performance Metrics** - Monitor route load times and re-renders\n\n### 2. Debug Mode Configuration\n\nEnable debug mode for detailed console logging:\n\n```tsx\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  defaultPreload: 'intent',\n  context: {\n    // your context\n  },\n  // Enable debug mode\n  debug: true,\n})\n```\n\n### 3. Browser DevTools Setup\n\n**Add router to global scope for debugging:**\n\n```tsx\n// In development only\nif (import.meta.env.DEV) {\n  window.router = router\n}\n\n// Console debugging commands:\n// router.state - current router state\n// router.navigate() - programmatic navigation\n// router.history - navigation history\n```\n\n---\n\n## Route Matching Issues\n\n### Problem: Route Not Found (404)\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- Route exists but shows 404 or \"Not Found\"\n- Console shows route matching failures\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Check Route Path Definition**\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Common mistake - missing leading slash\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: 'about', // Should be '/about'\n  // ...\n})\n\n// ✅ Correct\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/about',\n  // ...\n})\n```\n\n2. **Verify Route Tree Structure**\n\n```tsx\n// Debug route tree in console\nconsole.log('Route tree:', router.routeTree)\nconsole.log('All routes:', router.routesById)\n```\n\n3. **Check Parent Route Configuration**\n\n```tsx\n// Ensure parent route is properly defined\nconst childRoute = createRoute({\n  getParentRoute: () => parentRoute, // Must return correct parent\n  path: '/child',\n  // ...\n})\n```\n\n### Problem: Route Parameters Not Working\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- `useParams()` returns undefined or wrong values\n- Route params not being parsed correctly\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Verify Parameter Syntax**\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Wrong parameter syntax\npath: '/users/{id}' // Should use $\n\n// ✅ Correct parameter syntax\npath: '/users/$userId'\n```\n\n2. **Check Parameter Parsing**\n\n```tsx\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/users/$userId',\n  // Add parameter validation/parsing\n  params: {\n    parse: (params) => ({\n      userId: Number(params.userId), // Convert to number\n    }),\n    stringify: (params) => ({\n      userId: String(params.userId), // Convert back to string\n    }),\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    const { userId } = Route.useParams()\n    console.log('User ID:', userId, typeof userId) // Debug output\n    return <div>User {userId}</div>\n  },\n})\n```\n\n3. **Debug Current URL and Params**\n\n```tsx\nfunction DebugParams() {\n  const location = useLocation()\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n\n  console.log('Current pathname:', location.pathname)\n  console.log('Parsed params:', params)\n\n  return null // Just for debugging\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Navigation Issues\n\n### Problem: Navigation Not Working\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- Links don't navigate\n- Programmatic navigation fails silently\n- Browser URL doesn't update\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Check Link Configuration**\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Common mistakes\n<Link to=\"about\">About</Link> // Missing leading slash\n<Link href=\"/about\">About</Link> // Wrong prop (href instead of to)\n\n// ✅ Correct\n<Link to=\"/about\">About</Link>\n```\n\n2. **Debug Navigation Calls**\n\n```tsx\nfunction NavigationDebug() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n\n  const handleNavigate = () => {\n    console.log('Attempting navigation...')\n    navigate({\n      to: '/dashboard',\n      search: { tab: 'settings' },\n    })\n      .then(() => console.log('Navigation successful'))\n      .catch((err) => console.error('Navigation failed:', err))\n  }\n\n  return <button onClick={handleNavigate}>Navigate</button>\n}\n```\n\n3. **Check Router Context**\n\n```tsx\n// Ensure component is inside RouterProvider\nfunction ComponentWithNavigation() {\n  const router = useRouter() // Will throw error if outside provider\n  console.log('Router state:', router.state)\n\n  return <div>...</div>\n}\n```\n\n### Problem: Navigation Redirects Unexpectedly\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- Navigating to one route but ending up somewhere else\n- Infinite redirect loops\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Check Route Guards**\n\n```tsx\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/dashboard',\n  beforeLoad: ({ context, location }) => {\n    console.log('Before load - location:', location.pathname)\n    console.log('Auth state:', context.auth)\n\n    if (!context.auth.isAuthenticated) {\n      console.log('Redirecting to login...')\n      throw redirect({ to: '/login' })\n    }\n  },\n  // ...\n})\n```\n\n2. **Debug Redirect Chains**\n\n```tsx\n// Add to router configuration\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    /* ... */\n  },\n  // Log all navigation events\n  onNavigate: ({ location, type }) => {\n    console.log(`Navigation (${type}):`, location.pathname)\n  },\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## Data Loading Problems\n\n### Problem: Route Data Not Loading\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- `useLoaderData()` returns undefined\n- Loading states not working correctly\n- Data not refreshing\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Check Loader Implementation**\n\n```tsx\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/posts',\n  loader: async ({ params, context }) => {\n    console.log('Loader called with params:', params)\n\n    try {\n      const data = await fetchPosts()\n      console.log('Loader data:', data)\n      return data\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error('Loader error:', error)\n      throw error\n    }\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    const data = Route.useLoaderData()\n    console.log('Component data:', data)\n\n    return <div>{/* render data */}</div>\n  },\n})\n```\n\n2. **Debug Loading States**\n\n```tsx\nfunction DataLoadingDebug() {\n  const state = useRouterState()\n\n  console.log('Route status:', {\n    status: state.status,\n    isLoading: state.isLoading,\n    matches: state.matches.map((match) => ({\n      routeId: match.routeId,\n      status: match.status,\n      isFetching: match.isFetching,\n    })),\n  })\n\n  return null\n}\n```\n\n3. **Check Loader Dependencies**\n\n```tsx\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/posts/$postId',\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    // Loader will re-run when params change\n    console.log('Loading post:', params.postId)\n    return fetchPost(params.postId)\n  },\n  // Add dependencies for explicit re-loading\n  loaderDeps: ({ search }) => ({\n    refresh: search.refresh,\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## Search Parameters Issues\n\n### Problem: Search Params Not Updating\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- URL search params don't update\n- `useSearch()` returns stale data\n- Search validation errors\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Check Search Validation Schema**\n\n```tsx\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/search',\n  validateSearch: (search) => {\n    console.log('Raw search params:', search)\n\n    const validated = {\n      q: (search.q as string) || '',\n      page: Number(search.page) || 1,\n    }\n\n    console.log('Validated search params:', validated)\n    return validated\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    const search = Route.useSearch()\n    console.log('Component search:', search)\n\n    return <div>Query: {search.q}</div>\n  },\n})\n```\n\n2. **Debug Search Navigation**\n\n```tsx\nfunction SearchDebug() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n  const currentSearch = Route.useSearch()\n\n  const updateSearch = (newSearch: any) => {\n    console.log('Current search:', currentSearch)\n    console.log('New search:', newSearch)\n\n    navigate({\n      to: '.',\n      search: (prev) => {\n        const updated = { ...prev, ...newSearch }\n        console.log('Final search:', updated)\n        return updated\n      },\n    })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <button onClick={() => updateSearch({ q: 'test' })}>Update Search</button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Performance Issues\n\n### Problem: Excessive Re-renders\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- Components re-rendering too often\n- Performance lag during navigation\n- Memory usage increasing\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Use React DevTools Profiler**\n\n```tsx\n// Wrap your app for profiling\nimport { Profiler } from 'react'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <Profiler\n      id=\"Router\"\n      onRender={(id, phase, actualDuration) => {\n        console.log(`${id} ${phase} took ${actualDuration}ms`)\n      }}\n    >\n      <RouterProvider router={router} />\n    </Profiler>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n2. **Optimize Route Subscriptions**\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Subscribes to all search params\nfunction MyComponent() {\n  const search = Route.useSearch()\n  return <div>{search.someSpecificField}</div>\n}\n\n// ✅ Subscribe only to specific field\nfunction MyComponent() {\n  const someSpecificField = Route.useSearch({\n    select: (search) => search.someSpecificField,\n  })\n  return <div>{someSpecificField}</div>\n}\n```\n\n3. **Monitor Route State Changes**\n\n```tsx\n// Add to router configuration\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    /* ... */\n  },\n  onUpdate: (router) => {\n    console.log('Router state updated:', {\n      pathname: router.state.location.pathname,\n      isLoading: router.state.isLoading,\n      matches: router.state.matches.length,\n    })\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Problem: Memory Leaks\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- Memory usage constantly increasing\n- Browser becomes slow over time\n- Route components not cleaning up\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Check Component Cleanup**\n\n```tsx\nfunction MyComponent() {\n  const [data, setData] = useState(null)\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const subscription = someService.subscribe(setData)\n\n    // ✅ Always clean up subscriptions\n    return () => {\n      subscription.unsubscribe()\n    }\n  }, [])\n\n  return <div>{data}</div>\n}\n```\n\n2. **Monitor Route Unmounting**\n\n```tsx\nfunction DebuggableComponent() {\n  useEffect(() => {\n    console.log('Component mounted')\n\n    return () => {\n      console.log('Component unmounted')\n    }\n  }, [])\n\n  return <div>Content</div>\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## TypeScript Issues\n\n### Problem: Type Errors with Router\n\n**Symptoms:**\n\n- TypeScript errors in route definitions\n- Type inference not working\n- Parameter types incorrect\n\n**Debugging Steps:**\n\n1. **Check Route Tree Type Registration**\n\n```tsx\n// Ensure this declaration exists\ndeclare module '@tanstack/react-router' {\n  interface Register {\n    router: typeof router\n  }\n}\n```\n\n2. **Debug Route Type Generation**\n\n```bash\n# Check if route types are being generated\nls src/routeTree.gen.ts\n\n# Regenerate route types if needed\nnpx @tanstack/router-cli generate\n```\n\n3. **Use Type Assertions for Debugging**\n\n```tsx\nfunction TypeDebugComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  const search = Route.useSearch()\n\n  // Add type assertions to check what TypeScript infers\n  console.log('Params type:', params as any)\n  console.log('Search type:', search as any)\n\n  return null\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Systematic Debugging Process\n\n### 1. Information Gathering\n\nWhen debugging any router issue, start by collecting this information:\n\n```tsx\nfunction RouterDebugInfo() {\n  const router = useRouter()\n  const location = useLocation()\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    console.group('🐛 Router Debug Info')\n    console.log('Current pathname:', location.pathname)\n    console.log('Search params:', location.search)\n    console.log('Router state:', router.state)\n    console.log('Active matches:', router.state.matches)\n    console.log('Route tree:', router.routeTree)\n    console.groupEnd()\n  }, [location.pathname])\n\n  return null\n}\n\n// Add to your app during debugging\n;<RouterDebugInfo />\n```\n\n### 2. Isolation Testing\n\nCreate minimal reproduction:\n\n```tsx\n// Minimal route for testing\nconst testRoute = createRoute({\n  getParentRoute: () => rootRoute,\n  path: '/debug',\n  component: () => {\n    console.log('Test route rendered')\n    return <div>Debug Route</div>\n  },\n})\n\n// Add to route tree temporarily\nconst routeTree = rootRoute.addChildren([\n  // ... other routes\n  testRoute, // Add test route\n])\n```\n\n### 3. Step-by-Step Debugging\n\n1. **Verify basic setup** - Router provider, route tree structure\n2. **Check route definitions** - Paths, parent routes, configuration\n3. **Test navigation** - Links, programmatic navigation\n4. **Validate data flow** - Loaders, search params, context\n5. **Monitor performance** - Re-renders, memory usage\n\n---\n\n## Browser Debugging Tips\n\n### Console Commands\n\n```js\n// In browser console (when router is on window)\n\n// Current router state\nrouter.state\n\n// Navigate programmatically\nrouter.navigate({ to: '/some-path' })\n\n// Get route by path\nrouter.getRoute('/users/$userId')\n\n// Check if route exists\nrouter.buildLocation({ to: '/some-path' })\n\n// View all registered routes\nObject.keys(router.routesById)\n```\n\n### Network Tab\n\nMonitor these requests when debugging:\n\n- **Route code chunks** - Check if lazy routes are loading\n- **Loader data requests** - Verify API calls from loaders\n- **Failed requests** - Look for 404s or failed API calls\n\n### React DevTools\n\n1. **Components Tab** - Find router components and inspect props\n2. **Profiler Tab** - Identify performance bottlenecks\n3. **Search for components** - Find specific route components quickly\n\n---\n\n## Common Error Messages\n\n### \"Route not found\"\n\n- Check route path spelling and case sensitivity\n- Verify route is added to route tree\n- Ensure parent routes are properly configured\n\n### \"Cannot read property 'useParams' of undefined\"\n\n- Component is likely outside RouterProvider\n- Route might not be properly registered\n- Check if using correct Route object\n\n### \"Invalid search params\"\n\n- Check validateSearch schema\n- Verify search param types match schema\n- Look for required vs optional parameters\n\n### \"Navigation was interrupted\"\n\n- Usually caused by redirect in beforeLoad\n- Check for redirect loops\n- Verify authentication logic\n\n---\n\n## Performance Monitoring\n\n### Enable Performance Tracking\n\n```tsx\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  context: {\n    /* ... */\n  },\n  onUpdate: (router) => {\n    performance.mark('router-update')\n  },\n  onLoad: (router) => {\n    performance.mark('router-load')\n    performance.measure('router-load-time', 'router-update', 'router-load')\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Monitor Route Loading Times\n\n```tsx\nconst route = createRoute({\n  path: '/slow-route',\n  loader: async () => {\n    const start = performance.now()\n    const data = await fetchData()\n    const end = performance.now()\n\n    console.log(`Loader took ${end - start}ms`)\n    return data\n  },\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Next Steps\n\nAfter debugging router issues, you might want to:\n\n- [How to Set Up Testing](./setup-testing.md) - Add tests to prevent regressions\n- [How to Deploy to Production](./deploy-to-production.md) - Ensure issues don't occur in production\n\n<!-- TODO: Uncomment as guides are created\n- [How to Optimize Performance](./optimize-performance.md)\n- [How to Set Up Error Monitoring](./setup-error-monitoring.md)\n-->\n\n## Related Resources\n\n- [TanStack Router DevTools](https://github.com/TanStack/router/tree/main/packages/router-devtools) - Official debugging tools\n- [React DevTools](https://react.dev/learn/react-developer-tools) - React-specific debugging\n- [Router Core Documentation](../overview.md) - Understanding router internals\n"}
